{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When you beat.</b> Like one who beats wheat, and it is a pa'al verb: יִחַבֹּט קַצַּח in the nif'al binyan, and likewise all the letters of אחעה״ר when the nif'al binyan is formed from them, and these are לֹא יַאֲצִיר and לֹא יַחְסֹן and לֹא יֵהָרֵג, יֵעָבֵד בּוֹ, יִרְאֶה כָּל זָכָרְךָ — for such is the rule." "<b>You shall not adorn.</b> You shall not seek the adornments, and they are the branches; and likewise וְעָשִׂיתָ בָדִים וְשִׁלְּחַתְ פְּאֵרוֹת (Isaiah 54:12). It is also written with alef. And if it is read with vav, and likewise נְאָדוֹת הַיַּיִן."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:44.168164306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}